Subject: [PATCH] an attack resolves its target again before reading its reaction

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

A worldserver SIGSEGV at AttackAction::Attack (src/Ai/Base/Actions/AttackAction.cpp:102
at the pin below): bot->IsFriendlyTo(target) walks the target's reaction through
Unit::GetReactionTo into Object::GetGuidValue and faults at address 0, because the
target's update-field array is already gone. The target reaches Attack() as a raw
Unit* out of an AI value ("current target", "duel target"), checked only for null
and IsInWorld(). Both checks passed on the crashed tick, and neither can see the
state that matters: the flag they read is not the array the reaction read
dereferences, so a unit that has been removed from the world or destroyed -
despawned creature, logged-out player, a unit that left for another map - passes
both and faults three calls later.

AttackMyTargetAction, in the same file, already does the safe thing: it hands
Attack() botAI->GetUnit(guid), a fresh ObjectAccessor resolution that answers
only for a unit on the bot's own map. Attack() itself never re-resolves, so
every other caller rides on the cached pointer. This patch moves the resolution
into Attack(): after the existing null refusal, the target is resolved again by
GUID through botAI->GetUnit(...), and a null answer (target gone, or on another
map) refuses the attack. The existing IsInWorld() refusal and everything below
it run on the resolved pointer, unchanged.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream mod-playerbots re-resolving the attack target by GUID inside
AttackAction::Attack (or dropping the raw-pointer AI values that feed it), so
the reaction read can only ever run on a unit the map still holds.

APPLIES TO

quadseven/mod-playerbots @ 40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130, on top of
local patches 0001-0019. Touches only AttackAction::Attack in
src/Ai/Base/Actions/AttackAction.cpp. tests/replay_attack_target.py in
mod-overseer compiles the real body, pinned and patched, against a lifetime
model of the map store and runs the departed-target and other-map cases.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/AttackAction.cpp b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/AttackAction.cpp
index 702b6a3..be4a709 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/AttackAction.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/AttackAction.cpp
@@ -63,6 +63,19 @@ bool AttackAction::Attack(Unit* target, bool /*with_pet*/ /*true*/)
         return false;
     }
 
+    // The target arrives as a raw pointer out of an AI value, and a value
+    // can outlive the unit it names: a despawned creature, a logged-out
+    // player, a unit that left for another map. The null check above and
+    // the IsInWorld() check below cannot see that state - the reaction
+    // read further down goes through the target's update fields, which
+    // are already gone by then, and faults. Resolve the target again by
+    // GUID, the way AttackMyTargetAction in this file already does: the
+    // accessor answers only for a unit on the bot's own map, so a target
+    // that is gone or elsewhere comes back null and is refused here.
+    target = botAI->GetUnit(target->GetGUID());
+    if (!target)
+        return false;
+
     if (!target->IsInWorld())
     {
         if (verbose)
